    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d594">

                <pb facs="0884" n="1392" xml:id="pg1392"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/9–1048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in the United Kingdom
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-09-11T13:00:00-04:00">September 11,
                            1948—1 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3604. For Ambassador. Department believes we are now in general agreement with.
                    British as their thinking is revealed in your 4057 Sept 10. Re paras 2 and 3
                    your telegram, Dept’s position is one of persistent hope that Palestine dispute
                    may be kept out of UN debate at this juncture. However, British are correct in
                    assuming in para 3 that it may be necessary to have UN GA or possibly SC give blessing to
                    any suggested settlement in order to enable leaders on both sides to carry their
                    public opinion to acquiesce in such settlement.</p>
                <p>Our 2593 [<hi rendition="#italic">3593</hi>] Sept 10<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d594-f1"/> will have answered para 5. Re para 6 we agree that
                    approaches to Arabs and Jews should be parallel rather than joint. Your para 9:
                    We have no objection if US and UK representatives call on Mediator together but
                    we prefer that representations be parallel and not identical.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
